# Example 37: Genome-scale colony - 4300-gene GRN + FBA closure (NEW)
# Every cell's expression is a row of ONE shared numpy matrix (4338 genes,
# ~10^4 sparse regulatory edges, RegulonDB scale) advanced by a single
# vectorized call per tick (doc/18-programmable-cell-population-simulation.md §13 Design 5).  Expression-triggered core
# genes gate their reaction upper bounds in per-cell dFBA, so a knocked-out
# gene is simply a never-triggered silent node (WT growth ~0.12/h, a pgi
# knockout collapses to 0).
#
# The engineered .helix layer overlays the background genome: crp is a
# *background* master-regulator name, so the constitutive engineered copy
# reads/writes the shared matrix (overlap nodes share one expression state);
# gfp reports the engineered regulon on top of the genome-scale background.
#
# Scale note: the genome GRN step is < 1 s/tick at 10^4 cells (the doc's
# performance gate, verified in tests/test_genome_scale.py); the run below
# is kept to 256 cells / 12 ticks so the per-cell dFBA LPs (~2 ms each) do
# not dominate.  The doc's full-scale config (5000 cells x 60 ticks with
# dfba=true) is the same genome with proportionally more LPs.

#genome source=synth-4300 tf_map=regulon grn_mode=sparse active_gene_budget=512
#genome seed=7

#promoter name=p_housekeeping strength=-0.4
#promoter name=p_crp strength=0.6
#gene name=crp promoter=p_housekeeping
ATG GCT GGT GCT TAA
#end
#gene name=gfp promoter=p_crp
ATG GCT GGT GCT TAA
#end
#regulate crp -> gfp strength=+1.0

#media nutrient=GLC concentration=10.0 diffusion_um2_s=300
#media nutrient=O2 concentration=0.25 diffusion_um2_s=1600

#config backend=population
#config population_size=256 grid_width=32 grid_height=32
#config dfba=true dfba_dt_h=0.1
#config signaling=true signal_threshold=10.0
#config crowding=true mechanics=force
#config seed=0
#config ticks=12
#config output=population_size,alive_count,triggered_genes,core_acetate_mm,edge_oxygen_mm
